  "id": "faintness",
  "term": "faintness",
  "definition": "Faintness is a partial or greater loss of consciousness, often accompanied by paleness, weakness, and troubled breathing. It may follow heavy exertion, emotional shock, or other central bodily changes; a full faint is described historically as syncope.",
